ce":"both","text":"This was after he had defeated Sihon king of the Amorites, who lived in Heshbon, and then at Edrei had defeated Og king of Bashan, who lived in Ashtaroth.","from":4},{"book":"DEU","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"At that time we took from the two kings of the Amorites the land across the Jordan, from the Arnon Valley as far as Mount Hermon—","from":1},{"book":"DEU","chapter":3,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"which the Sidonians call Sirion but the Amorites call Senir—","from":1},{"book":"DEU","chapter":3,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Jair, a descendant of Manasseh, took the whole region of Argob as far as the border of the Geshurites and Maacathites. He renamed Bashan after himself, Havvoth-jair, by which it is called to this day.","from":5},{"book":"JOS","chapter":11,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"to the kings of the north in the mountains, in the Arabah south of Chinnereth, in the foothills, and in Naphoth-dor to the west;","from":3},{"book":"JOS","chapter":13,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Beth-peor, the slopes of Pisgah, and Beth-jeshimoth—","from":3},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The latter five came as allies to the Valley of Siddim (that is, the Salt Sea).","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"7-24":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":1,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"amorites-h0567","name":"Amorites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanites","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"heth-h2845","name":"Heth","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Canaan","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"hivites-h2340","name":"Hivites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaan