","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"tirzah-h8656h","name":"Tirzah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24}],"words":[{"base":"H0259","lemma":"אֶחָד","tr":"e·chad","gloss":"one","lang":"h","inPassage":32,"uses":970},{"base":"H1008","lemma":"בֵּֽיתְ־אֵל","tr":"bet-el","gloss":"Bethel","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":142},{"base":"H8112","lemma":"שִׁמְרוֹן מְראוֹן","tr":"shim·ron me·r·on","gloss":"Shimron-meron","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"H1171","lemma":"בַּ֫עַל גָּד","tr":"ba·al gad","gloss":"Baal-gad","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H1756","lemma":"דֹּאר","tr":"dor","gloss":"Dor","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"H3091","lemma":"יְהוֹשׁוּעַ","tr":"ye·ho·shu·a","gloss":"Joshua","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":218},{"base":"H0794","lemma":"אֲשֵׁדָה","tr":"a·she·dah","gloss":"slope","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H2510","lemma":"חָלָק","tr":"cha·laq","gloss":"(Mount) Halak","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H4068","lemma":"מָדוֹן","tr":"ma·don","gloss":"Madon","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H0407","lemma":"אַכְשָׁף","tr":"akh·shaph","gloss":"Achshaph","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"So they brought the five kings out of the cave—the kings of Jerusalem, Hebron, Jarmuth, Lachish, and Eglon.","from":10},{"book":"JOS","chapter":11,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Now when Jabin king of Hazor heard about these things, he sent word to Jobab king of Madon; to the kings of Shimron and Achshaph;","from":19},{"book":"JOS","chapter":11,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So Joshua took this entire region: the hill country, all the Negev, all the land of Goshen, the western foothills, the Arabah, and the mountains of Israel and their foothills,","from":8},{"book":"JOS","chapter":11,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"from Mount Halak, which rises toward Seir, as far as Baal-gad in the Valley of Lebanon at the foot of Mount Hermon. He captured all their kings and struck them down, putting them to death.","from":7},{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"At that time Horam king of Gezer went to help Lachish, but Joshua struck him down along with his people, leaving no survivors.","from":12},{"book":"JOS","chapter":11,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now when Jabin king of Hazor heard about these things, he sent word to Jobab king of Madon; to the kings of Shimron and Achshaph;","from":20},{"book":"GEN","chapter":12,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"From there Abram moved on to the hill country east of Bethel and pitched his tent, with Bethel to the west and Ai to the east. There he built an altar to the Lord, and he called on the name of the Lord.","from":16},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":1,"verseEnd":2,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"In those days Amraphel king of Shinar, Arioch king of Ellasar, Chedorlaomer king of Elam, and Tidal king of Goiim went to war against Bera king of Sodom, Birsha king of Gomorrah, Shinab king of Admah, Shemeber king of Zeboiim, and the king of Bela (that is, Zoar).","from":23}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}